  <p class="references-section__body font-proxima">
    ¹ Under U.S. law (DSHEA 1994), supplements are not required to be proven safe or effective before sale, and FDA
    oversight is largely post-market. Documented cases of mislabeling, adulteration, and manufacturing violations show
    that baseline industry standards don’t always prevent quality or safety errors. (Sources: FDA, Congress, JAMA)
  </p>
</section>

